        {
          "commentId": "6878e60a-1a7f-4bc0-9df4-c1d849d5cebd",
          "text": "As the word of God, Holy Scripture is a direct and primary object of faith, just as\nthe revelations which came to the patriarchs, and the inspired sermons of the prophets\nand apostles, were direct and primary objects of faith for their original recipients. \n\n这里“a direct and primary object of faith”翻译为“信心直接而首要的对象”确实比“信心直接而首要的目標”要好一些。但是在中文语境中，仍然显得有点抽象。从这 Object 表达的含义来看，似乎有“根基”、“基础”的含义。可以再斟酌一下，如何翻译这个词组。",
          "status": "resolved",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-05T23:53:44.899Z",
          "resolvedAt": "2026-09-06T01:00:56.878Z"
        },
        {
          "commentId": "dd945efd-9d8c-49ab-8b99-e99fcb06b6cb",
          "text": "The faith which he requires is divine faith springing\nfrom a recognition that the basis on which the Christian confession rests—that is, the\ntestimony of Scripture—is God’s own infallible testimony to himself. The ground of\ndivine faith in the divine truth of what the Scriptures teach is thus the fact of their ‘divine\noriginall’\n, which is the source of their authority (that is, as Owen defines it, their ‘power\nto command and require obedience, in the name of God’13). \n\n这里似乎用倒了 basis, ground 来诠释前文中的 object 的作用。另外“认信”这个词，对我来说，比较陌生，是某个神学术语吗？",
          "status": "resolved",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-05T23:56:57.521Z",
          "resolvedAt": "2026-09-06T01:00:56.878Z"
        }
      ]
    },
