    {
      "pairId": "68cd92e9-6e69-5a59-b313-7113863f153c",
      "sourceBlockId": "28f21c98-7576-5500-b7d1-7ab81eeb43ce",
      "targetBlockId": "2819096a-07bf-559b-bb46-1ec85662ad2e",
      "sourceContentHash": "046cead9b7213967708eb45db06d0649a701948656d819eb97dfea59db3ecf5c",
      "targetContentHash": "437c219543d6172065fc021db39af683bd0e69db4d05e1eb53e74f72f2798d3f",
      "status": "approved",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-06T05:59:52.715Z",
      "approvedAt": "2026-09-06T05:59:52.715Z",
      "comments": [
        {
          "commentId": "e9c293e3-55e8-4b76-907e-7d84aed20edb",
          "text": "Though written in the usual dull style (dull even for him!)\nwhich Owen affected when writing about the Scriptures, this chapter is veritable\ndynamite, and deserves reading and re-reading by all who desire to prove the perspicuity\nof Scripture for themselves.\n欧文写到圣经时，常采用一种沉闷的风格——即使对他而言也算沉闷！——但这一章其实充满爆发力。凡想亲自验证圣经清晰性的人，都值得一读再读。\n\n这里的“这一章”应该是指脚注 30 所指向的章节。但也许距离这一句子有点远，读到的时候，已经忘记“这一章”指的是什么了。是否可以拆分，或者把代名词再次表述一遍，以便可以读的更明白一些。",
          "status": "resolved",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-06T00:48:01.910Z",
          "resolvedAt": "2026-09-06T01:00:56.878Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "pairId": "1ff7006b-e18d-5bed-960f-7fd78f5ece58",
      "sourceBlockId": "e7834ad2-5077-5cae-bc61-f9bab171607c",
      "targetBlockId": "06f4b163-89c1-5a09-9895-a20bd6a2beba",
      "sourceContentHash": "1d335c5f84c0f049b614597e27a63bff7bae7bd52da5745e5928b6ef6a53e6e9",
      "targetContentHash": "9ba07efeac2419397d7175623a659c0e3a083dd30585f0aaa881d9b2a7ba9d05",
      "status": "approved",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-06T05:59:55.909Z",
      "approvedAt": "2026-09-06T05:59:55.909Z",
      "comments": [
        {
          "commentId": "9a898870-e072-47bb-bec9-3ac975ffc28c",
          "text": "landscape 在这里，我认为原译者适时的使用“景观”和“风景”来区分，似乎比较有助于理解。",
          "status": "resolved",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-06T00:49:53.252Z",
          "resolvedAt": "2026-09-06T01:00:56.878Z"
        },
        {
          "commentId": "a34671b6-8e81-415f-bc93-5b4ac3999c42",
          "text": "Generally, Owen saw Scripture as consisting of doctrines (facts about God) and examples\nof their application—the doctrinal principles interpreting the narratives, and the\nnarratives illustrating the doctrinal principles. \n\n总的来说，欧文认为圣经由教义——关于神的事实——及其应用实例组成：教义原则解释叙事，叙事则说明教义原则。\n\n这种翻译方法，本身从含义上是合理的。但是读起来，会让听众感到拗口。可以尝试把这个句子拆分成短一些的句子，有一些部分即便有重复也没关系。",
          "status": "resolved",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-06T00:52:09.392Z",
          "resolvedAt": "2026-09-06T01:00:56.878Z"
        }
      ]
    },
